1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johan_Collett_Falsen
2 CONT
2 CONT Johan Collett Falsen (9 September 1817 – 2 September 1879) was a Norwegian jurist and politician.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT John Collett Falsen born in the town of Grimstad in Nedenes amt in southern Norway. He was the son of Hagbart Falsen and wife Aletta Fleischer. He was the grandson of Enevold de Falsen (1755–1808) as well as being the nephew of ad
2 CONC miral Jørgen Conrad de Falsen (1785–1849), statesman Christian Magnus Falsen (1782–1830) and county governor Carl Valentin de Falsen (1787–1852).
1 FAMS @F6000000004128427226@
1 RFN geni:6000000008725438660
1 SUBM @S6000000002438602110@
