1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Velma June Crews
2 CONT Daily Herald, The (Everett, WA)  |  8 February 2007
2 CONT WA United States
2 CONT Velma June Crews Velma June Crews, 90, died peacefully in her sleep Friday, February 2, 2007, at 5:05 a.m. at the Ray Hickey Hospice House in Vancouver, Washington. Velma was born June 1, 1916, in Tacoma, Washington, to Audrey Lee
2 CONC  Richmond and Trygve J. Magelsen. On September 9, 1936, she married Ralph (Pete) Crews, in Everett, Washington.They had two sons, Darryl (deceased) and Larry. Velma and Pete and their sons lived in Sitka, Alaska, for a number of y
2 CONC ears before returning to Everett, Washington. Having lost Pete in 1970, Velma supported herself as a waitress in the Seattle area, she was a natural and never lost her desire to serve her family and friends. Velma was preceded in 
2 CONC death by her parents; husband, Pete; son, Darryl; brother, Earl; and sister, Mildred. She is survived by her son, Larry, Karen Johnson; sister and brother-in-law, Donna and Jim Kinder; brother and sister-in-law, Jim and Faye Johns
2 CONC on; sister and brother-in-law, Mary Ellen and Frances Smith; grand-niece, Malaura Dunn; grandchildren, Judi Vrieling, Rhonda Pennington, Rick, Darren and Deanna Crews, Larry Crews, Jr., Carmen Roberts and Dana Woods. She is also s
2 CONC urvived by 13 great-grandchildren; and five great-great grandchildren. Services will be at 10 a.m., Saturday, February 10, 2007, at the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter Day Saints located at 2223 N.W. 99th Street, Vancouver, Washi
2 CONC ngton. Condolences may be sent to Malaura Dunn, 4707 N.W. Division Avenue, Vancouver, WA 98663.
2 CONT
2 CONT Copyright, 2007, The Daily Herald, Everett, WA. All
