1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Richard Fabian Stang (born 19 August 1955) is a Norwegian lawyer and a Norwegian politician for the Conservative Party.[1] He was Mayor of the city of Oslo from 2007 until 2015.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Fabian Stang
2 CONT 66th Mayor of Oslo
2 CONT
2 CONT In office
2 CONT 17 October 2007 – 21 October 2015
2 CONT
2 CONT Deputy
2 CONT Libe Rieber-Mohn
2 CONT
2 CONT Preceded by
2 CONT Svenn Kristiansen
2 CONT
2 CONT Succeeded by
2 CONT Marianne Borgen
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Personal details'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Born
2 CONT 19 August 1955 (age 66)
2 CONT Oslo, Norway
2 CONT
2 CONT Political party
2 CONT Conservative
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Early life and education'''
2 CONT Stang was born in Oslo. He is the son of Norwegian actress Wenche Foss[2] and entrepreneur Thomas Stang.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Career'''
2 CONT Stang was first elected Mayor of Oslo in 2007, and reelected in 2011.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 2012 Stang spoke out in favour of increased immigration.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Stang is a supporter of subsidies and perks for electric cars in the city.[5][6]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 2015 Stang lost the mayoral election to Socialist Marianne Borgen.[1][7]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
2 CONT * "Former Oslo mayor fights off depression" Views and News from Norway, Sep 29, 2016
2 CONT * "Power struggle broke out after Oslo's mayor resigned". Aftenposten. 2007-08-23. Archived from the original on 2008-03-29. Retrieved 2008-06-06.
2 CONT * "Oslo finally has mayor". Aftenposten. 2007-10-17. Archived from the original on 2011-06-29. Retrieved 2008-06-06.
2 CONT * "Oslo mayor welcomes immigrant boom". The Local, 14 March 2012
2 CONT * "In Oslo, Electric Cars Drive Bus Operators Crazy". Wall Street Journal, Ellen Emmerentze Jervell and John D. Stoll, May 20, 2014
2 CONT * "Tesla Sedan Roars Ahead in Norway". Wall Street Journal, Oct. 2, 2013
2 CONT * "Socialist Marianne Borgen Becomes Oslo’s New Mayor". The Nordic Page, 17.10.2015
2 CONT
2 CONT
