1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Donald K. Sandness, 86, of Canton died Thursday, October 3, 2013 at Sanford Canton-Inwood Hospital.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born July 25, 1927 on the family farm south of Canton, to Ole and Jenny (Halvorson) Sandnes. Donald attended country school, and started farming at a young age with his father.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Marcella Reiff on Sunday, January 30, 1949 at the Dell Rapids Methodist Church. Two daughters, JoAnn and Donna, were born to this union. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The couple lived and farmed north of Canton all their married life.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a member of Canton Lutheran Church, but also enjoyed fellowship at Springdale and Grand Valley Lutheran Churches. Donald was always very proud of his Norwegian heritage and enjoyed his many trips to Norway, as well as hosti
2 CONC ng many Norwegian visitors. He especially enjoyed his years singing with the Greig Male Chorus and many activities with the Sons of Norway. Donald was a wonderful "old time" dancer and met his bride at the Arkota Ballroom. In his 
2 CONC later years, watching the Lawrence Welk Show and any other polka show was his favorite pastime.
2 CONT
2 CONT Grateful for having shared his life are his two daughters; JoAnn Fitzpatrick of Sioux Falls and Donna (Jim) Crowl of Faribault, MN; three grandchildren: Lisa (Chris) Berg of Wayzata, MN, Kelly Fitzpatrick of Sioux Falls, and Cory 
2 CONC Fitzpatrick of Minneapolis; and three great-grandchildren: Keagen and Paxton Fitzpatrick and Max Berg. He is also survived by two sisters-in-law: Ivona Sandnes of Canton and Arlayne Grottveit of Wauwatosa, WI; as well as several n
2 CONC ieces and nephews and special friends (almost daughters) Nancy Garry of Harrisburg and Jane Sinning of Lee's Summit, MO. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Donald was preceded in death by his wife, Marcella, his parents, his sister, Helen, and brothers, John Omar I, John Omar II, and Harold Kenneth.
2 CONT
