1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sonja Louise Barth (born 21 May 1923 death 10 September 2016) was a Norwegian environmentalist. She, along with her husband Edvard K. Barth, particularly the work of mapping reindeer hunting, traffic, and settlemen
2 CONC t in Dovre Tracts and Rondane.  She has published a number of writings on the same subject.
2 CONT
2 CONT During WW2 she was part of the intelligence group XU. Her efforts are described in the book "Everything what mothers have fought - women in opposition from 1940 to 1945." 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Royal Court announced on 5 December 2008 that the king had appointed Barth knighted by 1st class Order of St. Olav "for her unselfish contributions to society."
